CORRECTNESS (full deck, not just the short equiv input)
  np1, np2, np4 all reach END RUN at TIME=29.8 with ERRTOT=-0.000829,
  DETOT=-0.001596 -- BIT-IDENTICAL. Spot-checked the per-T energy: np1==np4
  byte-for-byte through a hard-binary episode (T=16 E=-31.521070, T=18
  E=-38.139037, T=19 E=-39.902193; large |E| is the binary's binding energy,
  DE stays ~1e-4). Splitting the regular force across the two physical 2080s
  (np2: 1 rank/GPU; np4: 2 ranks/GPU) reproduces the single-GPU answer
  exactly -- identical sm_75 parts + rank-ordered Allgatherv.

